From 24b75a5854fb98d112a40379da3041280d34b530 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:17:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] usb: typec: altmodes/displayport: Notify HPD after
 reconfiguring with HPD high

A Configure command sent while the sink asserts HPD, for example after
writing a new pin assignment to sysfs, goes through USB Safe State and
switches the lanes. This tears down the DisplayPort main link, but the
sink keeps HPD asserted, so dp_altmode_configured() sends no hotplug
event and the DisplayPort driver is never told that it must check and
retrain the link. Partners are not required to send an Attention after
the Configure command, and the one seen here does not after switching
from pin assignment C back to D, so the display stays black.

Send an out-of-band "connected" event once the new configuration has
been applied to the mux, so that the DisplayPort driver can check the
link status and retrain.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/usb/typec/altmodes/displayport.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/altmodes/displayport.c b/drivers/usb/typec/altmodes/displayport.c
index 51c92dd88..dc2673834 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/altmodes/displayport.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/altmodes/displayport.c
@@ -220,6 +220,21 @@ static int dp_altmode_configured(struct dp_altmode *dp)
 			sysfs_notify(&dp->alt->dev.kobj, "displayport", "irq_hpd");
 			dp->pending_irq_hpd = false;
 		}
+	} else if (dp->hpd) {
+		int ret;
+
+		/*
+		 * A Configure command while HPD is asserted (for example a new
+		 * pin assignment written to sysfs) passes through USB Safe State
+		 * and switches the lanes, which tears down the DisplayPort main
+		 * link. The sink keeps HPD asserted, so nothing else tells the
+		 * DisplayPort driver: notify it once the new configuration is
+		 * in place, so that it can check the link and retrain it.
+		 */
+		ret = dp_altmode_notify(dp);
+		drm_connector_oob_hotplug_event(dp->connector_fwnode,
+						connector_status_connected);
+		return ret;
 	}
 
 	return dp_altmode_notify(dp);
